  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for careful, honest people who can explain risks clearly. They judge you by notes, discipline and ethics.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is understanding how your own computer and network work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and skills required for cyber security: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools summarise alerts and draft reports. Routine triage shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, ethics and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explain concepts and check; later, own decisions and responses.
  </p>

